$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 EF2 {
  coords 574.161 76.987 7291.685
  m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>"\
  "Enemy forces consist of <b>C Company, 3rd Battalion, Princess Patricia's Canadian Light Infantry (3 PPCLI)</b>, with approximately 32 personnel. They are currently staging at a barnyard southwest of Joutkallio and preparing to conduct an assault on our position as seen by our drone."\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>"\
  "• Canadian forces have 2x JLTVs equipped with .50cal HMGs, providing significant mobile direct-fire support and several unarmed which we doubt will be used due to how close they are already."\
  "• The enemy has a significant intelligence advantage, they know pretty much everything about us from strength, capabilities, and supplies."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "FIA"
  }
  m_iOrder 2
 }
 FF2 {
  coords 574.161 76.987 7291.685
  m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>"\
  "We are the remaining elements of an FIA company, consisting of a platoon+ of personnel. After several days of pursuit and repeated skirmishes with Canadian forces, we have been forced into the hamlet of Joutkallio and the surrounding terrain."\
  ""\
  "Our forces are concentrated around Joutkallio, with the main supply route to the west and dirt track to the south marking our current limits of movement."\
  ""\
  "If my drone is destroyed, my standing orders are to remain at the built-up area and defend it."\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>"\
  "• We have no armoured vehicle capabilities."\
  "• We possess organic offensive and reconnaissance drone capabilities. (1x MAVIC with 14x VOG25 impact grenades)"\
  "• The terrain around Joutkallio contains numerous large boulders providing hard cover across otherwise open ground."\
  "Sparse vegetation provides generally good observation, while numerous terrain depressions allow for concealed movement and rapid repositioning."\
  ""\
  "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>"\
  "• No reinforcements. We have been cut off and isolated."\
  "• Supplies are very limited after several days of movement and repeated skirmishes."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "FIA"
  }
  m_iOrder 3
 }
 MIS2 {
  coords 574.161 76.987 7291.685
  m_sTitle "Mission"
  m_sTextData "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>"\
  "Conduct a <b>DELIBERATE DEFENCE</b> to repel the advancing Canadian forces and prevent them from destroying our remaining cell."\
  ""\
  "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>"\
  "Canadian forces have pursued us for several days following the destruction of our company. Our escape routes have now been cut off and the enemy has finally caught up, leaving our remaining cell isolated within Joutkallio."\
  ""\
  "We are to establish a determined defence throughout the hamlet and surrounding terrain. Inflict as many casualties as possible. Preserve our remaining personnel and equipment where possible, but do not allow the Canadians to overrun our position without a fight. If we live through this attack we might be able to conduct a breakout."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "FIA"
  }
  m_iOrder 4
 }
 SIT2 {
  coords 574.161 76.987 7291.685
  m_sTitle "Situation"
  m_sTextData "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
  "DTL: 15/08/1990, 1200hr, Al-Hadra, Kuwait."\
  "Weather: Clear, visability 1km+, no forecast of change."\
  ""\
  "<h2>LORE</h2>  "\
  "Following the coalition invasion of Kuwait, Iraqi forces have begun a fighting withdrawal while attempting to delay the coalition advance and retain control of key urban areas. Although the front line continues to move rapidly, isolated pockets of resistance remain determined to hold strategically important positions."\
  ""\
  "Al-Hadra has become one such battleground. British forces have established a fortified compound within the city to coordinate operations and maintain control of the surrounding area. Its location allows coalition forces to observe enemy movement, secure key routes, and project influence across the city."\
  ""\
  "Known locally as CIMIC House, the compound has become a significant obstacle to Iraqi operations. As long as it remains in British hands, Iraqi forces are unable to move freely through Al-Hadra or fully secure the area."\
  ""\
  "With coalition forces continuing their advance elsewhere, Iraqi commanders have committed a large force to seize the compound before it can be reinforced. The garrison now faces a determined assault and must hold its position until the attack is broken."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "FIA"
  }
  m_iOrder 1
 }
}